{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"georgiaite-flawless-sawfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# `sign-review` can never persist an attestation while ANY other ticket is being written: the sign fence compares store-wide tracker HEAD, not the subject's generation\n\n## Symptom (reproduced, 2026-08-21/22)\n\n`rebar sign-review <id>` — the documented no-LLM recovery for a plan review that PASSED but whose attestation failed to persist — itself fails, permanently, leaving the ticket unclaimable (the plan-review claim gate needs a signed attestation):\n\n```\n{\"ok\": false, \"signed\": false, \"ticket_id\": \"111a-4626-8d2c-42bf\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n \"reason\": \"the attestation could not be persisted: plan review generation remained unstable after 3 attempts\"}\n```\n\nAffected: `111a-4626-8d2c-42bf`, `825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f`, `7931-faee-53ba-47b1` (each latest REVIEW_RESULT sidecar = PASS, 0 blocking; `review-plan --status` = `unsigned`). ~25 `sign-review` rounds over ~20 minutes, 4s apart, recovered none of them. A co-occurring symptom from `review-plan` on the same subsystem:\n\n```\nattest.py:202 sign_plan_review -> generation.py:291 raise PlanReviewGenerationError(exc.reason)\nrebar.llm.plan_review.generation.PlanReviewGenerationError: store-read-failure\n```\n\nThis is NOT bug `c083` (stray untracked tracker files): at reproduction time `git status --porcelain` on the tracker was EMPTY, including untracked.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`generation.sign_manifest` validates signing against **store-wide git state of the shared tracker** rather than against the subject's own generation — the exact quantity `PlanReviewGeneration` deliberately excludes from identity. Three sites, one mechanism:\n\n- **A.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py:292` — `if before != after:` compares whole-tracker `git rev-parse HEAD` across `collect()`. Measured `collect()` on an affected ticket: **3.3–3.7s** (independently 4.3–5.8s under load), so the fence demands a ~5–7s globally quiescent tracker.\n- **B.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/generation.py:335` — `locked_head != expected_after` compares a **pre-lock** HEAD sample (line 288) against a **post-lock** one. This is anti-correlated by construction: a rebar process only moves HEAD by committing under this lock, so whenever acquisition *blocks*, the wait ends precisely after a HEAD-moving commit. Contention makes this near-certain, not merely likely.\n- **C.** `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/relation_snapshot.py:145-146` — `tracker_head_sha` runs `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no` **without the write lock** and treats any tracked-dirty output as fatal. The canonical writer does `git add` then `git commit` as two subprocesses under its lock (`_store/event_append.py:174-206`); an unlocked reader landing in that gap sees a **staged** (`A `) entry and hard-fails to `store-read-failure` — routed to the **non-retryable** `PlanReviewGenerationError` at `generation.py:290-291`, outside the 3-attempt loop.\n\nThe store is never quiescent, and mostly not because of user work: over the last 120 tracker commits the **median inter-commit gap is 3s**, and **65/120 are rebar's own background enrichment-queue events** (`ENQUEUE_ENRICH`/`CLAIM_ENRICH`/`TICKET_DIGEST`/`DONE_ENRICH`), driven from the store write path itself (`_store/event_append.py::_maybe_enrich_drain`) and re-fed by `attest.sign_plan_review`'s post-sign `_enqueue_queue.enqueue` (`attest.py:212-215`). With `MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 3` (`generation.py:27`), no backoff and no jitter, the whole retry budget burns inside one contiguous churn episode. The result is not a transient: the advertised recovery is structurally unable to succeed, and the classifier still names `recovery_tool=\"sign_review\"` (`resign.py`), closing the loop into a permanently unclaimable ticket.\n\nInstrumented live run (unrelated tickets named in every invalidating commit; subject `7931` never changed):\n\n```\n[20:55:27] before=aa28b30e   <- CLAIM_ENRICH 9263-b404-cb6c-463f\n[20:55:32] after =f3a7dead   <- TICKET_DIGEST 9263  (attempt 1 invalidated)\n[20:55:37] after =11d8f1d8   <- DONE_ENRICH  9263  (attempt 2 invalidated)\n[20:55:42] after =f076f662   <- CLAIM_ENRICH 932d  (attempt 3 invalidated)\nRESULT: remained unstable after 3 attempts\n```\n\n## Proof — hermetic, single independent variable\n\nTemp git tracker; `collect()` stubbed to return a generation **identical** to `initial_generation`, so \"the plan changed\" is impossible by construction. Sole variable: whether an **unrelated** ticket commits during the attempt.\n\n| arm | condition | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | unrelated ticket committing every 1s | `PlanReviewGenerationRetryable: plan review generation remained unstable after 3 attempts` (3x `before != after`) |\n| B | tracker quiescent | `{\"signed\": True}` |\n| C | HEAD stable across before/after; one unrelated commit lands only during lock acquisition | 3x `after='under-lock-mismatch'`, then exhausted — isolating clause **B**, since `locked_generation is initial_generation` |\n\nSite **C** (`store-read-failure`) confirmed separately: with a writer reproducing the locked `add`→`commit` gap, **87/149 (58.4%)** unlocked `tracker_head_sha(..., ignore_untracked=True)` probes raised `store-read-failure` while the committed HEAD stayed perfectly readable.\n\nRivals killed: \"the plan/material drifted\" (generation identical by construction; also `resign_plan_review`'s staleness guard passed, and 6 back-to-back `collect()` calls under live churn were byte-identical) — that path raises `PlanReviewGenerationChanged`, a different exception. \"Purely environmental contention\" (arm B signs; and the churn is rebar's own unconditional background machinery). \"Regression from 790c\" — falsified: `790c`'s diff (`a4ff2801be`) does not touch `before`/`after`/`locked_head`.\n\n## Why it violates a stated contract (legitimacy: defect / incomplete implementation)\n\n1. `PlanReviewGeneration`'s docstring, `generation.py:30-46`: `relation_snapshot` and `ticket_store_revision` are `compare=False` **because** they are store-WIDE, \"so including them made an unrelated ticket's concurrent write abort signing even though the signed artifact was unchanged\".\n2. `generation.py:93-101`: \"store-wide equality false-cancels on unrelated tickets' writes (bug d70a)\".\n3. `tests/unit/test_plan_review_generation_scope.py:1` — the file's own title: *\"Signing must survive UNRELATED concurrent tracker writes.\"*\n4. Bug **`790c-a7a3-120a-42c8`** (closed) AC-1: \"A review-plan PASS during which only UNRELATED store writes land ... ends certified with no manual step.\"\n5. `sign_manifest`'s own docstring, `generation.py:270`: \"Sign only if one stable **generation** still equals the immutable initial baseline\" — it enforces store-wide HEAD stability instead, which is strictly stronger and unachievable under the concurrency `AGENTS.md` prescribes.\n\n**Why it shipped green:** the regression test that encodes invariant (3) monkeypatches the fence out of existence — `test_plan_review_generation_scope.py:41`, `monkeypatch.setattr(generation, \"tracker_head_sha\", lambda *a, **k: \"b\" * 40)`. With the store-wide quantity frozen to a constant, the test can never observe the fence firing, so it proves the scoping fix while the two remaining store-wide comparisons stay untested.\n\n## Defect origin\n\n`git log -S'if before != after'` and `-S'locked_head != expected_after'` each return exactly one commit: `94e605a29d` (2026-07-22 11:32, `rebar-ticket: 5967-4476-7f9f-442d`, \"Add phased plan-review attestations\") — the commit that introduced the fence.\n\nAttributed instead to **`d70a-d06e-aea0-4008`** (`7c3c08df88`, 2026-07-22 20:37, \"d70a: scope plan-review signing to subject+related material, not the whole store\"), ~9 hours later. d70a is the ticket whose *scope of work was exactly this correction*: its commit message diagnoses the class verbatim (\"Any commit to any ticket in the window ... made `require_plan_review_for_claim` unreliable in exactly the parallel decomposition rebar promotes\"), fixes the identity comparison — and then states the omission outright: **\"The within-attempt before/after head fence is unchanged.\"** The two remaining comparisons are of the same store-wide quantity, in the same function, ~40 lines below the field d70a changed. This is a divergence from what a mechanical blame would report (`5967`), recorded deliberately: `5967` introduced the code, but `d70a` created and shipped-past the obligation, and is the review a reader could plausibly have caught this in.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nSigning must be gated on the **subject's generation** (own material + direct related-material pins + phase/floor), which `collect()` already computes and which was measured deterministic under live churn — not on store-wide tracker HEAD. Concretely: unrelated tickets' commits must not invalidate an attempt (sites A and B), and another writer's transient staged index inside its own locked `add`→`commit` gap must not collapse an unlocked read to a non-retryable `store-read-failure` (site C).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `sign_manifest` signs successfully when only UNRELATED tickets commit to the shared tracker throughout the attempt — verified by a test that actually commits an unrelated ticket event inside the window, WITHOUT monkeypatching `tracker_head_sha` to a constant.\n- [ ] `sign_manifest` signs successfully when an unrelated commit lands during lock acquisition (the `under-lock-mismatch` path) — same no-freezing constraint.\n- [ ] A genuine change to the subject's own or direct related material still fails closed with `PlanReviewGenerationChanged` and names the changed component (unchanged behaviour; companion test).\n- [ ] `tracker_head_sha` no longer returns `store-read-failure` because another process has files staged inside its own locked `add`→`commit` window; a caller's genuinely dirty tracked worktree still fails.\n- [ ] `under_lock_check`'s two disjuncts are logged distinguishably (head-moved vs generation-drifted) instead of a bare `after=\"under-lock-mismatch\"` (`generation.py:335-336,348-353`) — 25 field retries produced no actionable signal because of this.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_plan_review_generation_scope.py` no longer freezes `tracker_head_sha`, so the invariant in its title is actually exercised.\n- [ ] The three stuck tickets (`111a-4626-8d2c-42bf`, `825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f`, `7931-faee-53ba-47b1`) recover via `rebar sign-review` with no LLM re-run.\n\n## Notes / out of scope\n\nAggravator, not the root cause, and worth its own ticket if pursued: `tracker_head_sha` -> `ticket_reads.ensure_fresh` -> `_store_sync.reconverge` can itself MERGE `origin/tickets` and move HEAD from inside the fence window (throttled to <=1/60s, `_engine_support/reads.py:232`), and `under_lock_check` calls `tracker_head_sha` **while holding the write lock**, so a reconverge firing there re-enters `write_lock` from its own holder.","id":"a83f-6348-a08c-401d","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"sign-review can never persist an attestation while any other ticket is being written: the sign fence compares store-wide tracker HEAD, not the subject's generation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787371473717178001,"uuid":"f48a41bb-e5cb-4146-b360-1148e390120b"}